From bf91f3e3f779f960f61b6f6170da07b96178ee97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:10:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix compaction races: deleted keys returning and reads
 failing

Compaction now copies live records without touching the index, registers
the new segment, then swaps each entry with a compare-and-set, so writes
and deletes that land during compaction win. Hints are written only for
swapped entries. Recovery tracks tombstones so a stale copy in a
compacted segment cannot bring a deleted key back after a restart.
Reads retry when compaction moved the key between lookup and read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KX6wPBi9MP3EznAPnbTCtU
